          'A 6-year-old girl with sickle cell disease (HbSS) is admitted to the pediatric rehabilitation unit 10 days after presenting with acute left hemiparesis and dysarthria. MRI/MRA confirmed a large right middle cerebral artery territory infarction secondary to moyamoya-pattern vasculopathy. She underwent emergent exchange transfusion and was stabilized in the PICU. She has a history of two prior hospitalizations for vaso-occlusive crises but no prior strokes. Her transcranial Doppler (TCD) velocities had been elevated (210 cm/s in the right MCA) on screening 3 months ago, and she was scheduled to start chronic transfusion therapy, but the appointment was missed. Her parents speak limited English (primary language Spanish) and are visibly anxious. The father quietly asks the nurse if the hospital will ask about their immigration status.',
